{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, pca_n2000) achieved 0.485 acc, while config_016 (multimodal, pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc, suggesting adding the image modality helps. However, we cannot yet tell how much of that gain comes from the image features themselves versus true cross-modal fusion. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the clean single-variable ablation of config_016 with RNA removed, directly measuring the image-only baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: establishing the image-only baseline is critical for interpreting all future multimodal results. If image-only is already ~0.50+, the multimodal gain is modest and we should prioritize other design axes (profile, encoder, fusion). If image-only is much lower (~0.35-0.40), fusion is genuinely powerful and we should invest remaining budget heavily in multimodal extensions. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design question (value of fusion) before committing 7 remaining experiments to a specific direction."
}

